                        "sense_id": "a0e250c6-3edc-30ac-9ddb-f56b44feba1f",
                        "entry_id": "2416e032-88e0-386b-a6a5-9af757699b0c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Undying or immortal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57ad1ea3-ca60-41d4-acf4-fbbc02569cf2",
                                "sense_id": "a0e250c6-3edc-30ac-9ddb-f56b44feba1f",
                                "text": "Like the deathless vampire who must repeat its stalk-and-kill cycle in order to satisfy a recurring blood hunger, the earliest film horrors cannibalized its literary ancestry again and again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4eac729-9882-4bcd-8eb7-9446395a6640",
                                "sense_id": "a0e250c6-3edc-30ac-9ddb-f56b44feba1f",
                                "text": "“Hey, how do I kill this guy anyway?” “Finn, you can't kill my Dad!” “Oh, I-I'm sorry. I didn't mean --” “No, you literally can't kill my Dad. He's deathless.” “Oh.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fedd762e-ac84-390f-bf8c-21a998a0f96a",
                        "entry_id": "2416e032-88e0-386b-a6a5-9af757699b0c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Guaranteed not to be lost or forgotten due to its importance or conspicuous excellence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b77310da-a45b-4a28-ba03-951c6a3cf022",
                                "sense_id": "fedd762e-ac84-390f-bf8c-21a998a0f96a",
                                "text": "Her novels are filled with unforgettable characters and deathless prose."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0053fe6a-d5b4-4e5c-a233-a99d7035aa45",
                                "sense_id": "fedd762e-ac84-390f-bf8c-21a998a0f96a",
                                "text": "\"We cannot do less than call it Ixodes Maloni. The very small inconvenience of being bitten, my young friend, cannot, I am sure, weigh with you as against the glorious privilege of having your name inscribed in the deathless roll of zoology.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd96b45d-f716-4246-af52-4dfb04857a0c",
                                "sense_id": "fedd762e-ac84-390f-bf8c-21a998a0f96a",
                                "text": "Finally, one voice in England proclaimed him a deathless dramatist and portrayer of character (Morgann) (<422)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
